# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TokenTicks environment
#
# Every variable here is PUBLIC. Vite inlines anything prefixed VITE_ into the
# browser bundle, so nothing secret belongs in this file. Secrets (the Supabase
# service-role key, the Lemon Squeezy webhook signing secret) are set on the
# Supabase Edge Function, never here.
#
# All of it is optional. With none of it set, the app runs as a fully working
# local token counter and cost dashboard: accounts and paid features report as
# unavailable rather than breaking.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Project settings -> API. Use the anon / publishable key, NOT service_role;
# the app refuses to start with a service_role key here and explains why.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Lemon Squeezy ----------------------------------------------------------
# The checkout base for your store, without a trailing variant id.
VITE_LEMON_CHECKOUT_URL=https://your-store.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy

# Variant ids from Product -> Variants. The Pro annual one is optional; without
# it the annual toggle falls back to monthly for that plan.
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_PRO_MONTHLY=
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_PRO_ANNUAL=
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_TEAM_MONTHLY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set on the Edge Function only — `supabase secrets set KEY=value`:
#
#   LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET   signing secret from the webhook settings
#   LEMON_TEAM_VARIANT_IDS         comma-separated Team variant ids, so a Team
#                                  purchase provisions Team and not Pro
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY      injected by the platform; do not set by hand
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
